  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Expanding, factorising, solving and rearranging — plus reading and sketching graphs. This is the strand that feeds directly into AS and A-Level, so the habits you build here matter well beyond the exam.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Definition 2.1 — Factorising a quadratic",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "To factorise \\( x^{2}+bx+c \\), find two numbers that <strong>multiply to \\( c \\)</strong> and <strong>add to \\( b \\)</strong>. They become the constants in \\( (x+p)(x+q) \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "figure",
        "figure": {
          "type": "fn",
          "title": "Algebra &amp; Graphs — Coordinate Curve & Tangent Analysis (2)",
          "xrange": [
            -4,
            4
          ],
          "yrange": [
            -3,
            9
          ],
          "fns": [
            {
              "fn": "x*x - 2",
              "color": "var(--fig-indigo)",
              "label": "f(x) = x² - 2"
            },
            {
              "fn": "2*x - 3",
              "color": "var(--fig-amber)",
              "dash": "4,4",
              "label": "Tangent at x = 1"
            }
          ],
          "points": [
            {
              "x": 1,
              "y": -1,
              "label": "(1, -1)"
            },
            {
              "x": 0,
              "y": -2,
              "label": "(0, -2)"
            }
          ]
        },
        "caption": {
          "en": "Coordinate graph of f(x) = x² − 2 and its instantaneous tangent line at x = 1.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
